1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Laios and crew are returning to the surface.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
I just don't want to lose any of you.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Me neither.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
While their bonds are growing ever stronger,

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
let's go back in time a bit.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
You're finally conscious.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Are you feeling all right?

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Your injuries weren't too severe.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
I had to use goat's blood to replace what you lost.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
It'll do for now, but you should return to town soon.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
It's good you weren't still in the water,

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
or you'd have been fish food.

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
You should be thankful to whoever pulled you out.

14
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Are you thinking what I am?

15
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Kuro!

16
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
I know this scent.

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Elf. Tall man. Half foot. Dwarf.

18
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
The ones who stole our treasure.

19
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
I had a feeling it was those guys!

20
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The revival fee, please.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Enough for the goat's blood is fine.

22
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,000
That's right.

23
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,000
We were...

24
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Assaulted by some fishmen.

25
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:18,000
I guess we must have died again.

26
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
This is plenty, thank you.

27
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
They're adventurers?

28
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Aren't you...

29
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Need something?

30
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,000
No.

31
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Let's go, Nomari.

32
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Right!

33
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Got a soft spot for dwarves?

34
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Hm?

35
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,000
You have no integrity.

36
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Hey, I don't use someone's height to determine whether or not I hang out with them.

37
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
That's so.

38
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Our food is gone!

39
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
It got stolen by those guys again!

40
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Food.

41
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Are you kidding me?!

42
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,000
It's so weird.

43
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
They always take all our food, but none of our money.

44
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Maybe they keep running out of it?

45
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
So annoying.

46
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
We really should teach them a lesson.

47
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
What's the plan, Kabru?

48
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Hmm.

49
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
There's no choice.

50
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Let's go back.

51
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Wait!

52
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
You're joking, right?

53
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Shouldn't we go after them?

54
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
We don't have any food, though.

55
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
So we shouldn't go any further.

56
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
How about we admit defeat for now?

57
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Like that guy said before he left, we have to be thankful that we're alive at all.

58
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
If that's what you want to do, I guess I'll stick with you.

59
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
I will, too.

60
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,000
If you promise you won't give up on finding those filthy criminals, then I'm fine to return.

61
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
I promise, Ren. Thanks.

62
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Koro will do what Mikbel does.

63
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Oh, man.

64
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
I can't believe we're not making any profit this time.

65
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:57,000
There's so much fog.

66
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Hey, be careful, everyone!

67
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:07,000
This fog didn't occur naturally.

68
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
It's from a monster.

69
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:16,000
A fish man?

70
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:21,000
There are so many of them.

71
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
I guess there's no choice.

72
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Come on!

73
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:36,000
The way it uses that axe seems familiar.

74
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
This swinging motion.

75
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
I know it all too well.

76
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
That's right.

77
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
This is...

78
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Shh.

79
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Everything's fine.

80
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Just calm down.

81
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Daya.

82
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
It's me.

83
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:59,000
This fog's illusion magic.

84
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,000
The confused one with their weapon drawn is Koro.

85
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
And the one zoning out across from him is home.

86
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
He has a habit of freezing up when things get a bit crazy.

87
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
The one who ran off is probably Mik.

88
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
So, the one that poses the most dangerous...

89
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Ren.

90
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
She's already in mid-chant.

91
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
She has the power to turn us all into ashes instantly.

92
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,000
The only peaceful way to stop a chanting magic user is...

93
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Ren.

94
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
You get it, right?

95
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
This is all an illusion.

96
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
It's too bad she looks like a monster.

97
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Now then.

98
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
In order to stop this fog that was conjured...

99
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Huh.

100
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:50,000
This isn't the right one.

101
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
This isn't the right one.

102
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Those who attack with weapons aren't casters.

103
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,900
They're always observing things from afar.

104
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:06,880
That one.

105
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,960
All right, all right.

106
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:22,780
We surrender.

107
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:26,020
So would you mind letting go of my mage friend?

108
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:27,860
Wait a minute.

109
00:05:28,380 --> 00:05:30,520
They're the corpse retrievers from upstairs.

110
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:33,820
I don't think this reunion is just a coincidence.

111
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,720
You guys followed us, right?

112
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:37,360
What do you mean?

113
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:41,000
It's more profitable to retrieve corpses from a deeper floor,

114
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:43,040
because the island pays more for it.

115
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:46,340
We were angry about our stuff being stolen.

116
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,140
And while we were trying to get back,

117
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:50,360
we went to a floor that was above our skill level.

118
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,940
So all they had to do was follow us,

119
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:55,060
and they would find more profitable corpses.

120
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:57,940
Oh, so annoying.

121
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,860
But you were a little too late.

122
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:01,760
When you found us,

123
00:06:01,940 --> 00:06:03,680
we'd already been revived by someone else,

124
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:05,380
and we were heading back to the surface.

125
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:07,000
It made you panic.

126
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,160
So you decided to use illusion magic

127
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,680
to turn us all against each other.

128
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,460
You're a little off base.

129
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:15,560
What we wanted was for you to catch up to the thieves.

130
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:18,440
Having you kill each other would have been the best scenario.

131
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:20,300
But it's really a shame.

132
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:22,300
We didn't think you'd die so quickly

133
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:24,060
from being attacked by mere monsters.

134
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:26,220
You're a little...

135
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:29,700
Infighting and stealing between adventurers is a crime.

136
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:32,120
I'm reporting you to the island lord.

137
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:35,780
How about we make a deal?

138
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:38,760
It'd be wasteful for you to go back empty-handed.

139
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:42,720
Two of my party members were unfortunately taken out.

140
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:45,060
Deliver them to the resurrection office.

141
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:48,160
You should earn a decent amount of money for doing that.

142
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:50,580
Those two were just unconscious.

143
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:55,840
We'll testify that they got attacked by fishmen.

144
00:06:56,180 --> 00:06:57,740
As for splitting the reward,

145
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,840
we're gonna take 40.

146
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:02,420
No, 30% of it.

147
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:03,660
How's that?

148
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,480
It's a pretty good deal, isn't it?

149
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:09,180
All right.

150
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:10,300
I'll do it.

151
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:12,960
Kabru.

152
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,600
Oh, damn you.

153
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,460
Yeah, that makes more sense.

154
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:30,160
I'm glad you did the right thing.

155
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:44,300
Humanoids are so easy to deal with.

156
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:46,760
Every single dwarf, gnome, and tallman,

157
00:07:46,940 --> 00:07:48,920
they all tend to have identical weak points.

158
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:51,260
They move their bodies in the same way, too.

159
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:54,000
It's too bad monsters aren't like that.

160
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:57,200
Kuro, go find Mika, bring him back, will ya?

161
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:57,800
Kuro!

162
00:07:58,700 --> 00:07:59,200
Kabru.

163
00:07:59,540 --> 00:07:59,720
Hmm?

164
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,180
What about him?

165
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:03,300
Please let me go, I swear to you!

166
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:05,640
I didn't know about any of this!

167
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:09,060
You don't aim to lift the dungeon's curse,

168
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:11,400
nor eradicate the monsters in here.

169
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:14,160
The number of people who make a living

170
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,960
by stealing from others keeps growing.

171
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:18,100
Good people from this island

172
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:19,540
will leave if this continues.

173
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:25,300
That's why I can't forgive people like you.

174
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:26,800
Have mercy!

175
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:46,300
Kabru?

176
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:46,900
Hmm?

177
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:49,460
Oh, sorry about earlier.

178
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:51,840
It was the first solution I could think of.

179
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:52,740
Hmm.

180
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:54,720
What are you saying?

181
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:55,880
You know what?

182
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:56,660
Never mind.

183
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:58,220
Okay, if you say so.

184
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:00,440
I feel like we're messing up

185
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:02,440
and not actually making any progress.

186
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:03,780
You're right.

187
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:05,860
And this is the result of all of that.

188
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:07,420
It's really the worst.

189
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:10,100
You could stand to be a bit more encouraging.

190
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:12,320
There's no point in sugarcoating it.

191
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,720
This is just the best we can do for right now.

192
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:15,360
Huh.

193
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:18,280
The Island Lord only sees this dungeon

194
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:19,420
as a profitable tunnel.

195
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:21,720
If the gold runs dry,

196
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:23,940
he thinks that monster leather and bones

197
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:24,680
would be enough.

198
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:27,260
But no one's gonna dive into a dungeon

199
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:28,820
that's been thoroughly searched through.

200
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:32,420
Maybe because the get-rich-quick dream disappears,

201
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:35,240
or the spirit of adventure isn't being met.

202
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,700
The population starts to decline,

203
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:39,320
and then...

204
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:41,260
dangerous monsters pour out of the dungeon.

205
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:44,980
That's how a countless number of towns

206
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:45,900
have been destroyed.

207
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,640
We have to lift this place's curse and fast.

208
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:52,260
The world doesn't need monsters and dungeons.

209
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:53,320
Yeah.

210
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,080
I'm starving.

211
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,140
Being revived does make you hungry, huh?

212
00:10:00,660 --> 00:10:01,140
Kabu!

213
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,280
Check it out!

214
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:03,860
Those guys were carrying

215
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,440
some pretty valuable things on them!

216
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:06,420
All right.

217
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:08,120
Let's only take their food,

218
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:09,720
and then sink the rest of it.

219
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:11,380
What? Why sink it?

220
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:14,340
If we take just everything,

221
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:16,260
it means we're no better than they are.

222
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:18,280
Once we're all finished,

223
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,680
how about we eat a little something?

224
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:21,220
Let's do it!

225
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:27,840
It's time for us to dig in!

226
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:29,480
Whoa!

227
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:31,400
Those guys were eating good!

228
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:33,940
I guess corpse retrievers get paid a lot.

229
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,920
Yeah, when you're making your own corpses

230
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:36,740
to take back.

231
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:39,460
And the Island Lord hasn't caught on to that?

232
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:41,240
There are actually inspections

233
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:43,160
when it comes to payments from the island.

234
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:45,100
But it seems like those guys

235
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:46,080
were getting around it.

236
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,800
It's honestly more likely

237
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,040
that there are a lot of people

238
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:52,700
working together behind the scenes.

239
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:54,440
Sounds like corruption.

240
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,100
They're digging their own graves

241
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:56,880
by doing that.

242
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:59,100
Should we try to report this?

243
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:01,100
I wouldn't expect the Island Lord

244
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:02,560
to come up with a good solution.

245
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:04,600
Only rookies like Donnie

246
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,740
would be affected by it.

247
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:07,700
If the Island Lord burst

248
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:08,720
after stuffing himself,

249
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:09,840
I wouldn't mind at all.

250
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,280
I'm pretty sure the Elves

251
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,800
would step in and take his place.

252
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:14,400
Yeah, so we still need him

253
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,880
to act as sort of a middleman.

254
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,920
We're dealing with a dwarf

255
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:19,960
and a tall man

256
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:22,040
and an elf and a half foot.

257
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:23,440
What are you muttering?

258
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:25,240
Those are the people in the party

259
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:27,100
that put the ghost warding spell on us.

260
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:29,100
Oh, the ones who stole our treasure.

261
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,940
The ones who stole our food.

262
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:32,560
There aren't very many parties

263
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:33,460
with an elf in them.

264
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:34,780
We might figure it out

265
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:35,860
if we narrow things down.

266
00:11:36,860 --> 00:11:38,320
Maybe it's Donnie and Fiona?

267
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,060
It's hard to believe

268
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:41,100
that those two were able

269
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:42,420
to make it to the third floor.

270
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:45,600
Having only four party members is odd.

271
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,400
It's more reckless than anything.

272
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,580
Hey, Holm or Ren,

273
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:51,720
look closer at this ghost-repelling spell.

274
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,720
Wait, you still have that thing on?

275
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:55,220
Well, yeah, it's evidence.

276
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:58,400
That magic's not in my area of expertise.

277
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:00,200
Let me see.

278
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:03,380
Hmm.

279
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:05,600
Honor student.

280
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:07,060
It's like something

281
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,280
right out of a textbook.

282
